    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d941">

                <pb facs="0751" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8168</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests, to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-26T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1916, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>521. Department’s 484, October 12, 8 p.m. Foreign Office replies soldiers under
                    Herrera’s command never worked mine and that Herrera ordered suspension of work
                    immediately after brought to his knowledge.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
